BLD-14: JOB_INT=64 adds no flags; CMake jobs use default options only.
Evidence: ci/env_makefile.sh case 64) exports JOBBUILDFLAGS unchanged; only 32-64 adds -DINTSIZE64 -DIDXSIZE64;
.gitlab-ci.yml matrix_64 has JOB_INT [64] only (tags 64bits); ci/build_cmake.sh passes no option.
Patched:
  JOB_INT=64-64 bash -c 'source ci/env_makefile.sh' -> env-64-64.txt:
    -O0 -g -fPIC -DINTSIZE64 -DIDXSIZE64 -DSCOTCH_MPI_ASYNC_COLL
  The new build_cmake_gcc_64 job's options were run locally on the patched tree ($W/cm64):
    cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON -DINTSIZE=64 -DIDXSIZE=64
          -DSCOTCH_NAME_SUFFIX=_64 -DSCOTCH_DETERMINISTIC=FULL; make -j4; ctest -j4
    results in $W/verify-cm64.status
  64-bit Makefile build (-DINTSIZE64 -DIDXSIZE64) with make check / ptcheck: $W/verify.status (build64).
Runner architectures behind the 32bits/64bits tags cannot be verified from the repository.
